<title>SOUTH KOREA: S.Korea's KFA buys 30,000 tonnes of Indian soymeal.</title>
<headline>S.Korea's KFA buys 30,000 tonnes of Indian soymeal.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1996-12-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Korea's Korea Feed Association (KFA) bought 30,000 tonnes of Indian soymeal at $304.50 a tonne, C&amp;F, traders said on Thursday.</p>
<p>They said KFA bought the soymeal from G.Premjee soymeal with shipment for January 1-25 though a private negotiation.</p>
<p>Out of the total, 20,000 tonnes would be shipped to the port city of Inchon and 10,000 tonnes to Kunsan.</p>
<p>-- Seoul Newsroom (822) 727 5651</p>
